From bf628fe5515ea13a3ba368111cf982a1f59ca496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 16:08:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] riscv: defconfig: a210: skip the vector-misaligned boot
 probe

v7.1 enables RISCV_PROBE_VECTOR_UNALIGNED_ACCESS by default, which runs a
boot-time benchmark (schedule_on_each_cpu -> check_vector_unaligned_access)
that executes misaligned vector loads/stores on every CPU to classify their
speed. On the A210's heterogeneous XuanTie cluster (C908 + C920) this wedges
a core partway through: the probe completes and reports "slow" on the first
CPUs, then one core hangs executing the misaligned vector access, the
schedule_on_each_cpu sync never finishes, and the box dies with an RCU
expedited-grace-period soft lockup before reaching userspace:

  watchdog: BUG: soft lockup - CPU#4 stuck for 70s! [rcu_exp_gp_kthr:17]
   smp_call_function_single -> __sync_rcu_exp_select_node_cpus
  rcu: Possible timer handling issue on cpu=6 ... timer wakeup didn't happen

Select RISCV_SLOW_VECTOR_UNALIGNED_ACCESS instead: keep RISCV_ISA_V enabled
but assume slow misaligned vector access (matching what the cores that did
finish the probe reported) rather than probing for it. No boot probe, no
hang; hwprobe reports vector misaligned as slow.

Equivalent runtime workaround for testing: boot with
"unaligned_vector_speed=slow".

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig b/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
index e557444529077..958870accf304 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
+++ b/arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig
@@ -46,6 +46,10 @@ CONFIG_SMP=y
 CONFIG_NR_CPUS=16
 CONFIG_NUMA=y
 CONFIG_XUANTIE_ISA=y
+# v7.1's boot-time vector-misaligned probe (RISCV_PROBE_VECTOR_UNALIGNED_ACCESS)
+# wedges a XuanTie core on the A210, hanging SMP/RCU. Assume slow instead of
+# probing (matches what the cores that completed the probe reported).
+CONFIG_RISCV_SLOW_VECTOR_UNALIGNED_ACCESS=y
 CONFIG_RISCV_SBI_V01=y
 # CONFIG_SUSPEND is not set
 CONFIG_PM=y
